{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batch"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncSequences","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Batch","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Batch","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO5BatchV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchStrategy","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent13BatchStrategyP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent13BatchStrategyP7ElementQa"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When to emit the gathered elements; its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence’s, inferred from the call.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"strategy"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of the upstream’s elements, in order, in arrays of one or more.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The strategy decides when the pending elements are flushed: every so many elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/count(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), every interval"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/time(interval:clock:tolerance:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), on a signal or a unit of work"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), whenever any of several does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/either(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), or by a rule of your own ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). After every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flush, each strategy starts over. A flush with nothing pending emits nothing; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence never emits an empty array."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the upstream finishes, the pending elements, if any, are emitted as a last array and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the sequence finishes. When the upstream throws, the pending elements are dropped and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence throws the same error. A signal that finishes stops firing while the batches go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on; a signal that throws ends the sequence with its error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream and the strategy run in tasks of their own, started when iteration begins,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and arrays the consumer hasn’t taken yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are buffered. Cancelling the consumer, or dropping its iterator, cancels both. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"upstream or signal that ignores cancellation keeps the internal task alive until its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pending "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" returns, and is not read again after that; the batched sequence itself"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends at once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Batching needs iOS 16, Mac Catalyst 16, macOS 13, tvOS 16, watchOS 9 or visionOS 1."}]},{"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","text":"Example","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["for try await batch in [1, 2, 3, 4].async.batch(strategy: .either(.count(3), .time(interval: .seconds(1), clock: ContinuousClock()))) {","    print(batch) \/\/ Prints [1, 2, 3], then [4]","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any error the upstream or the strategy throws.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Gathers elements into arrays and emits each array when the strategy says to flush.","type":